**[Section 10: Events of Default]{.underline}**

Each of the following shall constitute an \"Event of Default\" under the DIP Facility:

> \(a\) Failure by the Borrower to satisfy any Milestone by the applicable date set forth in Section 9 hereof;
>
> \(b\) Variance from the Court-approved Budget in excess of plus or minus ten percent (±10%) on total disbursements, or variance in excess of plus or minus ten percent (±10%) on total receipts, in each case measured on a rolling two-week basis;
>
> \(c\) The filing by the Borrower, or the entry of an order, to convert the Chapter 11 case to a case under Chapter 7 of the Bankruptcy Code, or the filing of a motion to dismiss the Chapter 11 case;
>
> \(d\) The appointment of a Chapter 11 trustee or the appointment of an examiner with expanded powers beyond those set forth in Section 1106(a)(3) and (4) of the Bankruptcy Code;
>
> \(e\) The filing of a motion by the Borrower, or any order entered by the Bankruptcy Court, authorizing, approving, or permitting any alternative, supplemental, or replacement debtor-in-possession financing;
>
> \(f\) The termination or lapse of the Borrower\'s exclusive period to file a plan of reorganization under Section 1121 of the Bankruptcy Code, or entry of an order terminating or reducing the Borrower\'s exclusivity period, for any reason whatsoever;
>
> \(g\) The entry of an order granting relief from the automatic stay under Section 362 of the Bankruptcy Code with respect to any asset or assets of the Borrower having an aggregate value in excess of \$500,000;
>
> \(h\) The filing by any party in interest (including the Official Committee of Unsecured Creditors, any creditor, or any other party) of a challenge, objection, adversary proceeding, or other action contesting the validity, enforceability, priority, perfection, or amount of the DIP Lender\'s pre-petition second-lien claims or liens under the Pre-Petition Second Lien Credit Agreement, at any time after the expiration of the Investigation Period (as defined herein, being 60 calendar days from the date of formation of the Official Committee of Unsecured Creditors);
>
> \(i\) The occurrence of any event or condition that, in the sole discretion of the DIP Lender, could reasonably be expected to have a material adverse effect on the business, assets, liabilities, financial condition, results of operations, or prospects of the Borrower or any other Loan Party (a \"Material Adverse Change\");
>
> \(j\) Failure by the Borrower or any other Loan Party to pay any obligation under the DIP Facility when due, whether at maturity, by acceleration, or otherwise;
>
> \(k\) Any breach by the Borrower or any other Loan Party of any representation, warranty, or covenant contained in the DIP Loan Documents;
>
> \(l\) The entry of a final order by the Bankruptcy Court requiring the payment of any administrative expense claim or other claim that is *pari passu* with or senior in priority to the DIP superpriority claims (other than the Carve-Out as defined herein);
>
> \(m\) The entry of an order reversing, vacating, modifying, staying, or amending the Interim DIP Order or the Final DIP Order in any manner that is adverse to the DIP Lender, without the prior written consent of the DIP Lender;
>
> \(n\) The filing by the Borrower of any motion or pleading seeking to reverse, vacate, modify, stay, or amend the Interim DIP Order or the Final DIP Order without the prior written consent of the DIP Lender;
>
> \(o\) The entry of an order granting any lien on any DIP Collateral that is *pari passu* with or senior to the DIP Liens (other than Permitted Liens);
>
> \(p\) Any cross-default under the Pre-Petition Revolving Credit Facility or the Pre-Petition Second Lien Credit Agreement (to the extent applicable post-petition);
>
> \(q\) The entry of one or more final, non-appealable judgments against any Loan Party in an aggregate amount in excess of \$1,000,000 (to the extent not covered by insurance);
>
> \(r\) The occurrence of any ERISA Event (as to be defined in the DIP Credit Agreement) that could reasonably be expected to result in liability of any Loan Party in excess of \$1,000,000;
>
> \(s\) The occurrence of any material environmental event or violation of environmental laws at any facility owned or operated by any Loan Party;
>
> \(t\) Any change in the chief executive officer, chief financial officer, or chief restructuring officer of the Borrower without the prior written consent of the DIP Lender;
>
> \(u\) The entry of an order substantively consolidating the Chapter 11 case with the case of any non-Loan Party entity;
>
> \(v\) The cessation of operations at any manufacturing facility of any Loan Party without the prior written consent of the DIP Lender;
>
> \(w\) The failure to maintain insurance coverage as required under the DIP Loan Documents;
>
> \(x\) The filing of any motion by any party in interest seeking the appointment of an equity committee;
>
> \(y\) Any Loan Party shall become subject to a material regulatory action that could reasonably be expected to materially impair the value of the DIP Collateral;
>
> \(z\) The entry of an order approving the rejection of any executory contract or unexpired lease designated as a \"critical contract\" in the DIP Loan Documents without the prior written consent of the DIP Lender;
>
> (aa) The failure of the Borrower to deliver any Budget update, variance report, financial statement, or other required reporting within the applicable time period specified herein or in the DIP Credit Agreement; and
>
> (bb) Any other event or condition that is designated as an Event of Default in the DIP Credit Agreement or any other DIP Loan Document.

Upon the occurrence of an Event of Default, the DIP Lender may, in its sole discretion, (i) declare all outstanding DIP obligations immediately due and payable, (ii) terminate the DIP Facility commitments, (iii) exercise any and all rights and remedies available under the DIP Loan Documents, the DIP Orders, or applicable law, and (iv) deliver a Carve-Out Trigger Notice. The DIP Lender shall provide five (5) business days\' written notice to the Borrower and its counsel prior to the exercise of remedies, during which period the Borrower may seek an emergency hearing before the Bankruptcy Court, but the Bankruptcy Court shall not have the authority to condition the exercise of remedies on any showing other than the occurrence of an Event of Default.

**[Section 11: Credit Bidding and Sale Process]{.underline}**

**Credit Bid Rights.** The DIP Lender shall have the irrevocable and unconditional right to credit-bid the full amount of all outstanding DIP obligations (up to \$55,000,000 in aggregate, including both New Money Loans and Roll-Up Loans, together with all accrued and unpaid interest, fees, and other amounts payable under the DIP Facility) plus any and all outstanding pre-petition second-lien claims held by the DIP Lender (or its affiliates or designees) under the Pre-Petition Second Lien Credit Agreement, in any sale conducted under Section 363 of the Bankruptcy Code, any auction conducted in connection therewith, or any plan-related asset transfer, in accordance with Section 363(k) of the Bankruptcy Code. The Borrower shall not seek, support, or consent to any order or plan provision that would limit, restrict, or otherwise impair the DIP Lender\'s credit-bid rights, and any such limitation shall constitute an Event of Default.

**Stalking Horse Designation.** The Borrower shall designate the DIP Lender (or its designee, including any affiliate or entity controlled by or under common control with the DIP Lender) as the \"stalking horse\" bidder in any Section 363 sale process conducted during the Chapter 11 case. As stalking horse, the DIP Lender shall be entitled to customary bid protections, including without limitation:

> \(a\) A break-up fee equal to 3.5% of the proposed purchase price, payable to the DIP Lender (or its designee) in the event that the DIP Lender (or its designee) is not the successful bidder at any auction or is otherwise outbid; and
>
> \(b\) Expense reimbursement of up to \$2,000,000 for all reasonable and documented out-of-pocket fees, costs, and expenses incurred by the DIP Lender (or its designee) in connection with negotiating, documenting, and pursuing the stalking horse bid, including the fees of legal, financial, and other professional advisors, payable regardless of whether the DIP Lender (or its designee) is the successful bidder.

The stalking horse designation and the foregoing bid protections shall be included in any bidding procedures motion or sale procedures motion filed by the Borrower, and the Borrower shall use its best efforts to obtain Bankruptcy Court approval of such designation and protections. The Borrower shall not seek, support, or consent to any modification of the stalking horse designation or the bid protections described herein without the prior written consent of the DIP Lender.

The DIP Lender\'s credit-bid rights and stalking horse designation are fundamental elements of the DIP Facility and a material inducement for the DIP Lender to provide the financing described herein. The Borrower acknowledges that the DIP Lender\'s willingness to extend the DIP Facility is predicated in substantial part upon the rights set forth in this Section 11.

**[Section 12: Investigation Period and Lender Stipulation]{.underline}**

**Investigation Period.** The Official Committee of Unsecured Creditors (once appointed by the Office of the United States Trustee) shall have a period of sixty (60) calendar days from the date of its formation (the \"Investigation Period\") to investigate the validity, priority, enforceability, perfection, and amount of the DIP Lender\'s pre-petition second-lien claims and the liens securing the same under the Pre-Petition Second Lien Credit Agreement. During the Investigation Period, the Committee may, in its discretion, conduct such due diligence, review such documents, and take such other investigatory steps as it deems appropriate to evaluate the DIP Lender\'s pre-petition claims and liens.

Upon the expiration of the Investigation Period without the filing of a formal challenge, objection, complaint, or adversary proceeding by the Committee (or any other party in interest with standing to bring such a challenge) contesting the validity, enforceability, priority, perfection, or amount of the DIP Lender\'s pre-petition second-lien claims or liens, all rights to challenge, contest, avoid, or otherwise object to such claims and liens shall be deemed permanently and irrevocably waived by the Committee, the Borrower, the Borrower\'s estate, and all other parties in interest, and the DIP Lender\'s pre-petition claims and liens shall be deemed allowed and valid in all respects.

**Lender Stipulation.** As a condition precedent to entry of the Final DIP Order (as more fully described in Section 8 hereof), the Borrower and its estate shall stipulate, in the Final DIP Order or in a separate stipulation in form and substance satisfactory to the DIP Lender, to the validity, priority, enforceability, perfection, and amount of the DIP Lender\'s pre-petition second-lien claims in the aggregate principal amount of Ninety-Five Million Dollars (\$95,000,000), together with all accrued and unpaid interest and fees thereon, and shall irrevocably waive any and all rights to challenge, contest, avoid, or otherwise object to such claims or the liens securing the same (the \"Lender Stipulation\"). The Lender Stipulation shall not limit or prejudice the rights of the Committee during the Investigation Period, but the Borrower and its estate shall be bound by the Lender Stipulation immediately upon entry of the Final DIP Order.

**[Section 13: Reporting and Financial Covenants]{.underline}**

**Budget.** The Borrower shall deliver to the DIP Lender a 13-week cash flow budget (the \"Budget\") in form and substance satisfactory to the DIP Lender prior to the initial borrowing under the DIP Facility. The Budget shall set forth, on a week-by-week basis, all projected cash receipts, cash disbursements, and net cash flow for the Borrower and the Guarantors on a consolidated basis. The Budget shall be updated and delivered to the DIP Lender every four (4) weeks on a rolling 13-week basis, with each updated Budget subject to the review and approval of the DIP Lender.

**Budget Compliance.** The Borrower shall comply with the Budget, subject to permitted variances of plus or minus ten percent (±10%) on total receipts and plus or minus ten percent (±10%) on total disbursements, in each case measured on a rolling two-week basis. Any variance in excess of these permitted thresholds shall constitute an Event of Default under Section 10(b) hereof.

**Reporting Requirements.** The Borrower shall provide to the DIP Lender the following reports and information:

> \(a\) Weekly variance reports comparing actual cash receipts and disbursements to the Budget for the preceding week, delivered within five (5) business days after the end of each calendar week;
>
> \(b\) Monthly unaudited financial statements of the Borrower and its subsidiaries on a consolidated basis, including a balance sheet, income statement, and statement of cash flows, delivered within thirty (30) calendar days after the end of each calendar month;
>
> \(c\) Copies of all pleadings, motions, orders, and other documents filed in or issued by the Bankruptcy Court within two (2) business days of filing or entry; and
>
> \(d\) Such other reports, information, and data as the DIP Lender may reasonably request from time to time.

**Additional Covenants.** The DIP Loan Documents shall contain the following additional financial and operational covenants:

> \(a\) **Minimum Liquidity.** The Borrower shall maintain minimum liquidity (defined as unrestricted cash on hand plus available undrawn commitments under the New Money Revolving Facility) at all times in an amount to be specified in the DIP Credit Agreement;
>
> \(b\) **Capital Expenditure Limitation.** Total capital expenditures of the Loan Parties shall not exceed \$750,000 in the aggregate during any 13-week Budget period, unless otherwise approved in writing by the DIP Lender;
>
> \(c\) **Restrictions on Insider Payments.** No payments, transfers, distributions, or other remittances shall be made to any insider, equity holder, affiliate, or related party of any Loan Party without the prior written consent of the DIP Lender, except for ordinary-course compensation and benefits consistent with the Budget;
>
> \(d\) **Compliance with Law.** Each Loan Party shall comply in all material respects with all applicable laws, rules, and regulations; and
>
> \(e\) **Insurance.** Each Loan Party shall maintain in full force and effect all insurance coverage required under the DIP Loan Documents, with the DIP Lender named as loss payee and additional insured as applicable.

**[Section 14: Representations and Warranties]{.underline}**

The DIP Loan Documents shall contain customary representations and warranties for a debtor-in-possession credit facility of this nature, including without limitation the following:

> \(a\) Each Loan Party is duly organized, validly existing, and in good standing under the laws of its jurisdiction of organization and is qualified to do business in each jurisdiction where the nature of its business or ownership of its properties requires such qualification;
>
> \(b\) The execution, delivery, and performance of the DIP Loan Documents have been duly authorized by all necessary corporate or limited liability company action of each Loan Party, and the DIP Loan Documents constitute valid and binding obligations of each Loan Party, enforceable in accordance with their terms (subject to applicable bankruptcy and equitable principles);
>
> \(c\) No information furnished by any Loan Party to the DIP Lender in connection with the DIP Facility contains any material misstatement of fact or omits to state any material fact necessary to make the statements therein, in light of the circumstances under which they were made, not misleading;
>
> \(d\) Each Loan Party is in compliance in all material respects with all applicable laws, rules, regulations, and orders, including without limitation environmental, labor, tax, and ERISA requirements;
>
> \(e\) The DIP Liens are valid, binding, enforceable, and perfected first-priority priming liens on the DIP Collateral, subject only to Permitted Liens;
>
> \(f\) All financial statements delivered to the DIP Lender (including those audited or reviewed by Pinnacle Accounting LLP) present fairly in all material respects the financial condition and results of operations of the Borrower and its subsidiaries as of the dates and for the periods indicated;
>
> \(g\) There are no undisclosed liabilities or pending or threatened litigation, claims, or proceedings that could reasonably be expected to result in a Material Adverse Change;
>
> \(h\) Each Loan Party has good and marketable title to all of its material assets, free and clear of all liens, claims, and encumbrances other than Permitted Liens;
>
> \(i\) Each Loan Party is in compliance in all material respects with the requirements of ERISA and the Internal Revenue Code with respect to each employee benefit plan maintained or contributed to by such Loan Party; and
>
> \(j\) Each Loan Party has filed all material tax returns required to be filed and has paid all material taxes due and payable.

All representations and warranties shall be more fully set forth in the DIP Credit Agreement and shall be subject to customary exceptions, qualifications, and materiality thresholds as the parties may agree upon in the definitive documentation.

**[Section 15: Maturity and Termination]{.underline}**

**Maturity Date.** The DIP Facility shall mature, and all outstanding obligations thereunder shall be due and payable in full, on the earliest to occur of the following (the \"Maturity Date\"):

> \(a\) December 14, 2025 (i.e., nine (9) months from the anticipated Petition Date of March 14, 2025);
>
> \(b\) The effective date of a confirmed Chapter 11 plan of reorganization for the Borrower; or
>
> \(c\) The closing date of a sale of all or substantially all of the Borrower\'s assets pursuant to Section 363 of the Bankruptcy Code.

**Mandatory Prepayment.** The Borrower shall be required to make mandatory prepayments of the DIP Facility from the net cash proceeds of (a) any sale, transfer, or other disposition of assets of any Loan Party outside the ordinary course of business (other than any sale approved by the DIP Lender), (b) any casualty event or condemnation, and (c) any extraordinary receipts, in each case subject to customary exceptions to be set forth in the DIP Credit Agreement.

**Voluntary Prepayment.** The Borrower may voluntarily prepay the DIP Facility in whole or in part at any time without premium or penalty, *provided* that any voluntary prepayment shall be subject to the payment of the Exit Fee described in Section 4 hereof and any breakage costs associated with SOFR borrowings.

**Termination.** The DIP Facility shall terminate and all commitments of the DIP Lender shall expire upon the repayment in full of all DIP obligations, including all principal, accrued interest, the Exit Fee, and all other fees, costs, expenses, and other amounts payable under the DIP Loan Documents.

**[Section 16: Governing Law and Jurisdiction]{.underline}**

**Governing Law.** This Term Sheet and the DIP Loan Documents shall be governed by and construed in accordance with the laws of the State of New York (without giving effect to any choice-of-law or conflict-of-law provisions that would result in the application of the laws of any other jurisdiction), except to the extent that the Bankruptcy Code or other federal law is applicable.

**Jurisdiction.** The Bankruptcy Court shall have exclusive jurisdiction over all disputes, claims, and matters arising out of or relating to the DIP Facility, the DIP Loan Documents, or the transactions contemplated hereby. In the event the Bankruptcy Court abstains from exercising or declines to exercise jurisdiction over any such matter, or in the event the reference to the Bankruptcy Court is withdrawn, the United States District Court for the District of Delaware shall have jurisdiction over such matter.

**Waiver of Jury Trial.** Each party hereto irrevocably and unconditionally waives any and all rights to a trial by jury in any action, proceeding, or counterclaim arising out of or relating to the DIP Facility, the DIP Loan Documents, or the transactions contemplated hereby.

**[Section 17: Indemnification]{.underline}**

The Borrower and each Guarantor shall, jointly and severally, indemnify and hold harmless the DIP Lender, the DIP Agent, and each of their respective officers, directors, members, managers, employees, agents, advisors, representatives, and affiliates (including without limitation Marcus Holt, David Howe, and each professional of Pendleton Howe LLP and Ridgeline Advisory Group) (each, an \"Indemnified Person\") from and against any and all losses, claims, damages, liabilities, penalties, costs, and expenses (including reasonable attorneys\' fees and disbursements) arising out of or in any way relating to the DIP Facility, the DIP Loan Documents, the Chapter 11 case, or any transaction contemplated hereby, except to the extent that any such losses, claims, damages, liabilities, penalties, costs, or expenses are determined by a court of competent jurisdiction in a final, non-appealable judgment to have resulted primarily from the gross negligence or willful misconduct of such Indemnified Person. The indemnification obligations set forth herein shall survive the termination of the DIP Facility and the repayment of all DIP obligations.

**[Section 18: Miscellaneous / Additional Terms]{.underline}**

**Confidentiality.** This Term Sheet is confidential and proprietary to the DIP Lender and shall not be disclosed, distributed, or made available to any person or entity other than the Borrower, its board of directors, and its professional advisors (including Whitfield & Crane LLP, Stonebridge Partners LLC, Hartwell & Associates, and Pinnacle Accounting LLP) without the prior written consent of the DIP Lender, which consent may be withheld in the DIP Lender\'s sole discretion. Notwithstanding the foregoing, the Borrower may disclose this Term Sheet to the Bankruptcy Court in connection with the filing of the DIP Motion, subject to such confidentiality protections as may be appropriate.

**Exclusivity.** From the date hereof through the earlier of (a) the date on which the DIP Credit Agreement is fully executed and delivered by all parties thereto, or (b) April 1, 2025, the Borrower shall negotiate exclusively with the DIP Lender regarding debtor-in-possession financing and shall not, directly or indirectly, solicit, encourage, entertain, negotiate, or enter into any discussions or agreements with any other person or entity regarding any alternative, supplemental, or replacement debtor-in-possession financing, unless and until this Term Sheet is terminated in accordance with its terms.

**Non-Binding.** This Term Sheet is non-binding and does not constitute a commitment to lend, a binding agreement, or an obligation to provide financing. The DIP Lender\'s obligation to provide the DIP Facility is expressly conditioned upon the execution and delivery of definitive DIP Loan Documents in form and substance satisfactory to the DIP Lender, the entry of interim and final DIP Orders in form and substance satisfactory to the DIP Lender, and the satisfaction or waiver of all conditions precedent set forth herein and in the definitive documentation. The DIP Lender reserves the right to modify, supplement, or withdraw this proposal at any time prior to the execution of the DIP Credit Agreement.

**Definitive Documentation.** The DIP Credit Agreement and all other DIP Loan Documents shall be prepared by Pendleton Howe LLP, counsel to the DIP Lender, and shall be in form and substance satisfactory to the DIP Lender in all respects. The Borrower and its counsel shall cooperate fully in the negotiation, preparation, and execution of such documentation.

**Amendments.** Any amendments, modifications, or waivers of the terms of the DIP Facility, whether set forth in this Term Sheet, the DIP Credit Agreement, or any other DIP Loan Document, shall require the prior written consent of the DIP Lender and the Borrower, and Bankruptcy Court approval to the extent required by the DIP Orders or applicable law.

**[Section 19: Signature Block]{.underline}**

**IN WITNESS WHEREOF**, the parties have caused their duly authorized representatives to execute this Term Sheet as of the date first written above.

**IRONCLAD CAPITAL PARTNERS, LLC**, as DIP Lender and DIP Agent

